  "name": "Adrenaline",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-worn-brown.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "The thrill of danger burns in your blood like gas in a mantle. You gain Adrenaline whenever you do something Risky: use an ability marked Risky, move through a foe's tile, leap a gap or drop of 10' or more, or anything else the Dark Master judges could hurt you if it goes wrong. You gain it before you roll and keep it even if you fail. It lasts until the start of your next turn, and ends when the encounter ends. While you have Adrenaline, a foe you force to move into a prop (a wall, pillar, gas-main, heavy furniture or a creature larger than it) takes d6 damage.",
    "source": "feature",
